TargetParser: the default target triple without uname

Failure: lib/TargetParser/Unix/Host.inc does not compile for the C kit:
`'sys/utsname.h' file not found` (Host.inc:22); it calls uname() to add the
OS release to a Darwin triple and the AIX version to an AIX one.
Change: under LLVM_ABSD_KIT the header is not included, getOSVersion()
returns "" and the AIX branch is left out.
Behaviour preserved: the ABSD build's host and default triple is
x86_64-unknown-none-elf, which carries no OS version and is neither Darwin
nor AIX, so the result is the triple unchanged, as before. Other platforms
are unchanged.
Upstreamability: needs an ABSD OS in LLVM; as an "OS without uname" switch
it would be acceptable.

--- a/llvm/lib/TargetParser/Unix/Host.inc
+++ b/llvm/lib/TargetParser/Unix/Host.inc
@@ -19,7 +19,9 @@
 #include "llvm/Config/config.h"
 #include <cctype>
 #include <string>
+#if !defined(LLVM_ABSD_KIT)
 #include <sys/utsname.h>
+#endif
 
 #ifdef HAVE_UNISTD_H
 #include <unistd.h>
@@ -28,12 +30,18 @@
 using namespace llvm;
 
 static std::string getOSVersion() {
+#if defined(LLVM_ABSD_KIT)
+  // The kit has no uname; ABSD's triple (x86_64-unknown-none-elf) carries
+  // no OS version, so there is none to add.
+  return "";
+#else
   struct utsname info;
 
   if (uname(&info))
     return "";
 
   return info.release;
+#endif
 }
 
